<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-GB>Horrible, terrible – ask the wind f=
or
recipes instead, this shit would make me head-butt a unicorn until into a
lobotomy.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-GB>So – I wrote, and am writing, this.=
 <br>
Expect typos – and unless the typo is a fucking slur or complexly
unrecognizable – I’m probably not going to be fucked to fix it. </span><span
lang=3DEN-GB style=3D'font-family:"Segoe UI Emoji",sans-serif;mso-ascii-fon=
t-family:
Calibri;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-font-family:Calibri;
mso-hansi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-char-type:symbol-ext;mso-symbol-font-f=
amily:
"Segoe UI Emoji"'>&#128522;</span><span lang=3DEN-GB><o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-GB>Okay? Okay! <br>
<br>
Also – this is not a copy of the handbook – I won’t re-explain every single
recipe, especially for recipes with many <span class=3DSpellE>varaints</spa=
n>.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-GB><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><span lang=3DEN-GB>Also, in-game, I like to keep a <i>=
narrator
tone </i>– expect more swearing.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span lang=3DEN-GB style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;line-h=
eight:
107%'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></b></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span lang=3DEN-GB style=3D'font-size:16.0pt;line-h=
eight:
107%'>Hydrocarbons.<br>
</span></b><span lang=3DEN-GB>While I won’t explain every distillation in d=
etail,
if petroleum is important enough to murder each other in the real world, I
suppose it’s only fair I explain it a little in the context of Boric Alchem=
y. <br
style=3D'mso-special-character:line-break'>
<![if !supportLineBreakNewLine]><br style=3D'mso-special-character:line-bre=
ak'>
<![endif]><b><o:p></o:p></b></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span lang=3DEN-GB>Oily Rocks are functionally an o=
re</span></b><span
lang=3DEN-GB>. They are deposits of crude oil squeezed into porous rocks, l=
ike limestone,
shale, or sandstone.<br>
These rocks must be crushed and fired in a <b>retort </b>to get petroleum.<=
o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal><b><span lang=3DEN-GB>Petroleum </span></b><span lang=
=3DEN-GB>must
be run through a fractional distiller to extract the fractions within.<br>
As of writing this document, these fractions are: <br>
<b>Gasoline</b> (good solvent, fuel for flamethrowers and grenades), <br>
<b>Naphtha</b> (feedstock for plastic alcohols and carboxylic acids), <br>
<b>Diesel</b> (very energy-dense fuel),<br>
<b>Carbolic Oil</b> (can be made into phenol, cresols, or nepheline. Useful=
 for
synthetic dye),<br>
<b>Mineral Oil</b> (can replace fat in many vanilla recipes – but not the o=
ne
where it’s supposed to burn),<br>
<b>Paraffin Wax </b>(can replace bees wax in many <span class=3DGramE>vanil=
la</span>
